          %p
            Via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            of such correspondences by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
            of adjacent legs, they form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Span"} Span
          %p
            Assuming some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊢
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast \vdash f_\ast
          %ul
            %li
              %em push-forward
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast \,\colon\, \mathcal{D}(X) \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}(A)
          %p and
          %ul
            %li
              %em pull-back
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast \,\colon\, \mathcal{D}(A) \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}(X)
          %p
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functorially
            associated with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            (i.e. such that there are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_2 f_1)_\ast \,\simeq\, (f_2)_\ast (f_1)_\ast
            and dually), the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+transform"} integral transform
            encoded by any span as above is the “pull-push” operation given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_* f^*
          %p
            Now the Beck-Chevalley condition (on such assignment of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            adjoints to maps) essentially says that this pull-push construction is (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"}> 2-
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functorial
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            of
            = succeed ":" do
