          %p
            This
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BCConditionInMotivationFromIntegralTransform"} (1)
            is the Beck-Chevalley condition: A natural necessary condition to ensure that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+transforms"} integral transforms
            by pull-push
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            through
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            is functorial under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
            of adjacent legs.
          %p
            More motivation along these lines also be found at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type+theory"} dependent linear type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            this is
            %a{:href => "dependent+linear+type+theory#Schreiber14"} Sc14
            there.
          %h3#MotivationFromLogicAndTypeTheory From logic and type theory
          %p
            From the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+logic"} formal logic
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_! \dashv f^\ast \vdash f_\ast
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            constitute the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantification"} quantification
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantification"}> existential quantification
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+pair+type"} dependent pair type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊣
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context+extension"} context extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊣
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantification"} universal quantification
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+type"} dependent product type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+variables"} free variables
            commutes with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantification"} quantification
            — a condition which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntactically
            is “self-evident”, at least it is evidently desirable.
          %p
            Original articles with this logical perspective on the BC condition:
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Lawvere70"} Lawvere (1970), p. 8
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Seely83"} Seely (1983), p. 511
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Pavlović91"} Pavlović (1991), §1
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Pavlović96"} Pavlović (1996), p. 164
          %p
            For more on this logical aspect see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#InTypeTheory"} below
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Suppose given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+square"} commutative square
            (up to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            = succeed ":" do
