                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_!
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wirthm%C3%BCller+context"} Wirthmüller context
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            that makes the square commute
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k^* f^* \to h^* g^*
          %p
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mate"} mate
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h_! k^* \to g^* f_!
          %p defined as the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi η
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi ϵ
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h_! k^* \overset{\eta}{\to} h_! k^* f^* f_! \overset{\cong}{\to} h_! h^* g^* f_! \overset{\epsilon}{\to} g^* f_!
                  \\,.
          %p
            We say the original square satisfies the
            %strong Beck–Chevalley condition
            if this mate is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            More generally, it is clear that for this to make sense, we only need a transformation
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^* f^* \to h^* g^*
            %em Beck–Chevalley condition
            in this case,
          %h3#left_and_right_beckchevalley_condition Left and right Beck–Chevalley condition
          %p
            Of course, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^*
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^*
            also have
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints"} left adjoints
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_! h^* \to f^* g_!
            is an isomorphism, and this is not equivalent in general. Context is usually sufficient to disambiguate, although some people speak of the “left” and “right” Beck–Chevalley conditions.
          %p
            Note that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^* f^* \to h^* g^*
            is not an isomorphism, then there is only one possible Beck-Chevalley condition.
          %h3#dual_beckchevalley_condition Dual Beck–Chevalley condition
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^*
            have
            %em right
            adjoints
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^* f_* \to h_* k^*
            is an isomorphism. By adjointness, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^*
            have right adjoints and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^*
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^*
            have left adjoints, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^* f_* \to h_* k^*
            is an isomorphism if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_! h^* \to f^* g_!
            is.
          %p This proves the following statement.
          %p
          #DualExactSquare.num_cor
            %h6 Corollary
            %p Consider a square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{A &amp; \overset{g^*}{\to} &amp; C\\
                    ^{f^*}\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow^{h^*}\\
                    B &amp; \underset{k^*}{\to} &amp; D}
            %p
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^*
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^*
              have left adjoints and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^*
              have right adjoints. The square satisfies the Beck-Chevalley condition (meaning that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_! h^* \to f^* g_!
              is invertible) exactly if the opposite square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{A^\op &amp; \overset{(f^\op)^*}{\to} &amp; B^\op \\
                    ^{(g^\op)^*}\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow^{(k^\op)^*}\\
                    C^\op &amp; \underset{(h^\op)^*}{\to} &amp; D^\op}
            %p
              satisfies the Beck-Chevalley condition (meaning that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi op
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h^\op)_! (k^op)^* \to (g^\op)^* (f^\op)_!
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^* f_* \to h_* k^*
          %h3#for_bifibrations For bifibrations
          %p
            Originally, the Beck-Chevalley condition was introduced in (
            %a{:href => "#BenabouRoubaud70"}> Bénabou-Roubaud, 1970
            ) for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibrations"} bifibrations
            over a base category with pullbacks. In
            %em loc.cit.
            they call this condition
            %strong Chevalley condition
            because he introduced it in his 1964 seminar.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X} \to \mathbf{B}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
            has pullbacks satisfies the
            %strong Chevalley condition
            iff for every commuting square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi ψ
                                %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                                  %mo ′
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi φ
                                %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                                  %mo ′
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi φ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi ψ
                        %mtd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ &amp; \overset{\psi^\prime}{\rightarrow} &amp; \\
                  \\downarrow^{\varphi^\prime} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\varphi}\\
                  \&amp; \underset{\psi}{\rightarrow} &amp; }
          %p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
            over a pullback square in the base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphism"} cartesian
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            is cocartesian it holds that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi φ
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi^\prime
            is cartesian iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^\prime
            is cocartesian. Actually, it suffices to postulate one direction because the other one follows. The nice thing about this formulation is that there is no mention of “canonical” morphisms and no mention of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cleavages"} cleavages
          %p
            A fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            has products satisfying the Chevalley condition iff the opposite fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^{op}
            is a bifibration satisfying the Chevalley condition in the above sense.
          %p
            According to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benabou%E2%80%93Roubaud+theorem"} Benabou–Roubaud theorem
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+descent"} monadic descent
          %h3#Local “Local” Beck–Chevalley condition
          %p
            Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^*
            do not have entire left adjoints, but that for a particular object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            the left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!(x)
            exists. This means that we have an object “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_! x
            ” and a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_x\colon x \to f^* f_! x
            which is initial in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x / f^*)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo *
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^*(\eta) \colon k^* x \to k^* f^* f_! x \to h^* g^* f_! x
            %em
              local Beck-Chevalley condition at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^*(\eta)
            is initial in the comma category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo *
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k^* x / h^*)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^* f_! x
            as “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_! k^* x
            ” (although we have not assumed that the entire functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_!
            exists).
          %p
            If the functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_!
            do exist, then the square satisfies the (global) Beck-Chevalley condition as defined above if and only if it satisfies the local one defined here at every object.
          %h2#InTypeTheory In logic / type theory
          %p
            If the functors in the formulation of the Beck-Chevalley condition are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            functors in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            (or just of a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi h
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi g
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  D &amp;\stackrel{h}{\to}&amp; C
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{k}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                  \\\
                  A &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; B
                  }
          %p
            is interpreted as a morphism of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contexts"} contexts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
            or of fibers in a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^*
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            is interpreted as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
            in these contexts. And the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi k
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_k \coloneqq k_!
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi q
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_q \coloneqq g_!
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            is interpreted (up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} (-1)-truncation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} existential quantification
          %p
            In terms of this the Beck-Chevalley condition says that if the above diagram is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %strong substitution commutes with existential quantification
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi g
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_k h^* \phi \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} f^* \sum_g \phi
                  \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Consider the diagram of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contexts"} contexts
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo :
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo :
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo :
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Γ
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo :
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo ,
                                %mi t
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 3
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Γ
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi id
                                %mo ,
                                %mi t
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    [\Gamma, x : X] &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; [\Gamma, x : X, y : Y]
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Gamma &amp;\to&amp; [\Gamma, y : Y]
                    }
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\simeq
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    \\Gamma \times X &amp;\stackrel{(p_1,p_2,t)}{\to}&amp; \Gamma \times X \times Y
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{p_1}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{(p_1,p_3)}}
                    \\\
                    \\Gamma &amp;\stackrel{(id,t)}{\to} &amp; \Gamma \times Y
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              with the horizontal morphism coming from a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo :
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t : \Gamma \to Y
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              and the vertical morphisms being the evident
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              substitute
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              before or after quantifying over
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sum_{x : X} \phi(x,t) \simeq (\sum_{x : X} \phi(x,y))[t/y]
                    \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#various Various
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
                of any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
                is a bifibration, and satisfies the Beck–Chevalley condition at every pullback square. In particular,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+categories"} locally cartesian closed categories
                always satisfy the Beck–Chevalley condition.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
                (such as a
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(C) \to C
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
                satisfies the Beck–Chevalley condition at every pullback square.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+fibration"} family fibration
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Fam
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fam(C)\to Set
                of any category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                with small sums satisfies the Beck–Chevalley condition at every pullback square in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "double+coset#MackeyFormula"} Mackey’s restriction formula
                for group representations.
          %h3#images_and_preimages Images and pre-images
          %p
          #BeckChevalleyForPreImageBetweenPowerSets.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Beck-Chevalley for images and pre-images of sets)
              %br/
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \,\in\, Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(S)
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
              regarded as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(S)
                  is the set of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset S
              %li
                %p
                  regarded as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                  by declaring that there is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
                  precisely if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset B
                  as subsets of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \,\colon\, S \longrightarrow T
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              between sets, we obtain the following three
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              between their
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi f
